WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.294 --> 00:00:05.531
Miles Hendon ran out into the alleyway near the inn, but there was no sign

2
00:00:05.532 --> 00:00:09.039
of Edward. He spent the whole day trying to track down the boy. He remembered the

3
00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:13.206
threats John Canty had made, and it frightened him. "The poor boy must be scared

4
00:00:13.207 --> 00:00:19.287
out of his wits," Miles said to himself. Then he paused to think. "No .

5
00:00:19.288 --> 00:00:27.931
. . Unlike most boys his age, he has bravery and maturity&#8212;I've no doubt he

6
00:00:27.932 --> 00:00:34.014
will escape from Canty." It was well into the night by now. Miles found a nearby

7
00:00:34.015 --> 00:00:40.686
inn and quickly fell asleep. Early the next morning, he lay thinking of where Edward

8
00:00:40.687 --> 00:00:44.754
might go when he managed to get free of Canty. "He's a clever boy. Surely

9
00:00:44.755 --> 00:00:53.322
he'll leave London . . . "I've got it! I am his only friend in the

10
00:00:53.323 --> 00:01:00.076
world. He knows I am heading to Hendon Manor! Yes, that is where the boy

11
00:01:00.077 --> 00:01:07.908
will go!" Miles jumped out of bed. "I'll wait for him there!" He dressed quickly

12
00:01:07.909 --> 00:01:12.990
and started his journey home. Edward, meanwhile, wanted nothing more than to be at home too&#8212;his

13
00:01:12.991 --> 00:01:21.661
home, the palace where he had grown up. But instead he was being dragged through

14
00:01:21.662 --> 00:01:31.462
dark alleys and backstreets again. "I said I'd find you, didn't I?" Canty laughed spitefully.

15
00:01:31.463 --> 00:01:36.552
"You'll obey everything I say from now on." "I obey no one! I am the

16
00:01:36.553 --> 00:01:42.365
king, and I give the orders! I order you to release me this instant!" Edward commanded.

17
00:01:42.366 --> 00:01:47.298
But Canty just sneered, pulling at the king of England even harder. Leaving the city

18
00:01:47.299 --> 00:01:51.792
behind, they came upon an old barn. Canty made a whistling sound. The barn door

19
00:01:51.793 --> 00:01:57.278
creaked open, and a man in shabby clothes approached them. The man eyed Edward up and

20
00:01:57.279 --> 00:02:06.619
down. "He doesn't look like much." "He brings in more in one day than you

21
00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:15.755
make in a week, Hugo!" Canty spat. "I am not some object!" Edward interjected. "How

22
00:02:15.756 --> 00:02:23.255
dare you treat me this way! You will pay the harshest penalty for this!" Hugo stared

23
00:02:23.256 --> 00:02:30.418
at Edward and then chuckled. "Your son is a ball of fire! Maybe he can

24
00:02:30.419 --> 00:02:36.504
work for us." "I am not his son! I no longer have a father," Edward

25
00:02:36.505 --> 00:02:42.754
said sadly. "He's bumped his head or something." Canty laughed nervously as he pushed Edward

26
00:02:42.755 --> 00:02:48.084
into the barn. Edward withdrew to a quiet corner, covered himself in hay, and closed his

27
00:02:48.085 --> 00:02:51.398
eyes. "I have to get to the palace," he thought. His present ordeal was unbearable.

28
00:02:51.399 --> 00:02:58.570
But what he found even more excruciating was that he would never see his father

29
00:02:58.571 --> 00:03:05.227
again. That night he cried himself to sleep. Soon Edward was awakened by loud singing and

30
00:03:05.228 --> 00:03:10.723
laughter. To his surprise, the barn was empty. Edward crept to the door and carefully

31
00:03:10.724 --> 00:03:15.547
opened it. He cringed as it creaked loudly. "Just in time to meet the others!"

32
00:03:15.548 --> 00:03:20.557
said Hugo, who had been standing guard. "Others?" Edward stepped outside. Now he could hear music.

33
00:03:20.558 --> 00:03:25.696
A large group of men, women, and children were dancing and singing merrily. From their

34
00:03:25.697 --> 00:03:31.185
manner of dress, Edward guessed they were a band of vagrants. Canty was talking to

35
00:03:31.186 --> 00:03:36.938
a man with an eye patch. Hugo pushed Edward toward the men. "Come here, boy&#8212;let

36
00:03:36.939 --> 00:03:43.945
me have a look at you," said the man with the patch. He seemed to be

37
00:03:43.946 --> 00:03:48.112
chief of this gang. "Yes, you could be of some use." Before Edward could speak,

38
00:03:48.113 --> 00:03:55.592
another man ran up to the chief. "The newcomers want to pay their respects," he

39
00:03:55.593 --> 00:03:59.252
said, pointing to a group of men who waited in the shadow of the trees. "What's

40
00:03:59.253 --> 00:04:04.101
their story?" asked the chief. "Their farms were taken from them to be changed into

41
00:04:04.102 --> 00:04:10.505
sheep ranges. They begged to stay, but they were whipped and thrown off their own

42
00:04:10.506 --> 00:04:13.828
land," explained the man. The chief nodded. "Bring them here!" As the men approached, the chief

43
00:04:13.829 --> 00:04:21.408
stared at a man with welts on his arms. "What happened?" he said. "I lost

44
00:04:21.409 --> 00:04:27.244
my farm and went begging to feed my children. For that I was whipped. Now

45
00:04:27.245 --> 00:04:35.396
my family's vanished, and I hope they are anywhere but this cruel place called England!"

46
00:04:35.397 --> 00:04:39.726
He spat on the ground. "I am Victor," chimed in a man who walked with a

47
00:04:39.727 --> 00:04:45.902
limp. "I too had my own land until the earl decided to use it for

48
00:04:45.903 --> 00:04:52.368
his horses. The farm had been in my family for many generations. Now we have

49
00:04:52.369 --> 00:04:55.971
nothing." "What happened to your leg?" asked the chief. "When I said I wouldn't give up

50
00:04:55.972 --> 00:05:06.452
my land, the king's guards pushed me so hard I fell and broke my leg.

51
00:05:06.453 --> 00:05:12.454
It has never healed properly." Edward could not believe what he was hearing. "This cannot

52
00:05:12.455 --> 00:05:19.880
be true!" he thought. "I assumed these men were hoodlums, good-for-nothings. Yet they seem to be

53
00:05:19.881 --> 00:05:28.372
victims of injustice." A man with long hair spoke next. "I'm Peter. I escaped from

54
00:05:28.373 --> 00:05:32.529
the king's guards while being transported to another dungeon." "With what crime were you charged?"

55
00:05:32.530 --> 00:05:36.348
asked the chief. "Stealing a gentleman's watch," Peter answered. "Did you steal it?" said the

56
00:05:36.349 --> 00:05:39.186
chief. Peter grinned and replied, "Of course!" Then he grew sober again. "I would pay for

57
00:05:39.187 --> 00:05:44.509
my crime if the punishment fit. But I will not die for such a minor

58
00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:51.065
offense. So I'm forced to hide for the rest of my life. I can't contact

59
00:05:51.066 --> 00:06:02.258
my family, and I have no friends." Peter looked away, a sullen expression on his face.

60
00:06:02.259 --> 00:06:14.825
"You are among friends now," the chief told him. "We've all experienced in one way

61
00:06:14.826 --> 00:06:23.645
or another the manner with which our king looks after his people," he added bitterly.

62
00:06:23.646 --> 00:06:28.474
"The king does not consider us worthy of his care. But I say, are we not

63
00:06:28.475 --> 00:06:41.876
citizens of England also?" "Yes, you are!" Edward thrust himself into the midst of the

64
00:06:41.877 --> 00:06:50.537
group. "From this day forth, injustice and cruelty will stop. I will not tolerate such

65
00:06:50.538 --> 00:06:55.187
things. In England all men will be treated with equality and respect!" The people who

66
00:06:55.188 --> 00:07:03.193
had been singing and dancing turned to gape at the young boy standing there with his

67
00:07:03.194 --> 00:07:09.208
right hand held up in a solemn promise. "And who might you be, little boy?"

68
00:07:09.209 --> 00:07:13.345
asked the chief. Edward straightened up. "I am Edward, king of England," he said with

69
00:07:13.346 --> 00:07:19.436
dignity. A loud burst of laughter followed. A few people came over to clap Edward on

70
00:07:19.437 --> 00:07:22.764
the back. "Good joke, boy!" "But I am telling you the truth!" shouted Edward. "I

71
00:07:22.765 --> 00:07:31.749
am the king!" The chief wiped tears of laughter from his eyes. "Obviously you need

72
00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:44.243
a title, and I'm going to give you one. Everybody!" he called. "May I introduce to

73
00:07:44.244 --> 00:07:51.581
you Foo-Foo the First. He's the king&#8212;king of the Mooncalves!" "Foo-Foo! Foo-Foo!" People started chanting

74
00:07:51.582 --> 00:07:57.315
the ridiculous name. Edward spun away from them, tears of anger and indignation filling his

75
00:07:57.316 --> 00:08:03.397
eyes. He'd offered to change the law of England, and all they were doing was

76
00:08:03.398 --> 00:08:09.143
making fun of him! Still, Edward found himself feeling a grudging respect for this gang of

77
00:08:09.144 --> 00:08:14.839
thugs. The men might be vagrants and thieves, but they exhibited loyalty to one another.

